target/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
.tmp/
*.log

# Working notes for a session: screenshots, `uiautomator dump` output, one-off probes.
# Kept on disk because they answer "what did the screen actually look like", which is
# the one question a log cannot. Never worth a commit.
.workbuddy/

# Plan.md 进仓库（2026-11-24 用户拍板）：它不只是工程日志，还是唯一能把
# 「为什么是这个设计、哪些结论被实测证伪过」讲清楚的文档，丢了不可再生。

# Release signing. The key already lives outside the tree; this keeps its password
# and any stray keystore that gets dropped in here from reaching the archive, where
# the only fix is rotating the key for every clone.
android/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore

# Packet captures: every question they can answer has already been turned into a
# number in the notes, and the count keeps growing as new questions show up. The
# scripts that read them are worth a commit (they are the argument); the bytes
# underneath are not - GitHub refuses a single file over 100 MB anyway. Kept on
# disk (now under .workbuddy/tmp), readable by the committed scripts, never in
# the tree.
*.pcap

# Python leaves these behind the first time anyone runs a probe.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Module payload backups: every `*.ko.gz` is a gzip of a whole driver build (the
# big ones ~5 MB, the small ones tens of KB), and each experiment that swapped one
# left a copy behind (`.bak`, `.prev`, `.selfbuild-backup`, `.eac-keep`, ...).
# What matters for reproducing a number is *which* fingerprint ran, and that is
# recorded as text in `kernel/README.md` and in Plan.md - the bytes themselves
# answer nothing the sha256 does not. The payloads that ship (assets/kernel in the
# APK, registered in kernel/PAYLOAD.sha256) are the un-suffixed `*.ko.gz`, which
# stay tracked.
kernel/*.ko.gz.*

# 本机的 SDK 位置（P1-21）：每台机器自己写，不进仓库。构建从 ANDROID_HOME 派生。
android/local.properties

# fuzz 的运行期产物：corpus 会越长越大，artifacts 是崩溃输入（发现即修，不留库）。
fuzz/corpus
fuzz/artifacts
fuzz/coverage
fuzz/target
